35,2,1,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, the past is surprisingly honest. Four lift rebuilds finished on time, but two lane-priority stretches were reverted. History suggests we should avoid traffic experiments.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, history is a poor substitute for current capacity. My rosters show the late-turn pool is hollowed out; overtime is masking a structural void.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, your staffing concerns are valid. My audits show waiting for connections costs the most minutes, not ticket queues. We must fix the transfers, not the machines.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, your focus on transfers is wise. My committee minutes show ferry and rail data terms are still unresolved. We must know who else must say yes before we begin.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, your caution is vital. My ledger shows a ring-fenced construction balance, but operating subsidies are trimmed. We must avoid plans that rely on volatile operating funds.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,May,,"@Midori, your transfer insight is sharp. My pilot data shows the late-evening timetable actually hit its cost target. We should trust proven schedules, not new tech.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, proven schedules are useless if no one is left to run them. My crew data shows a third below establishment. We cannot promise what we cannot staff.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, I hear your worry. But my timed runs show platforms clear at old rates. The bottleneck is connection waiting, not crowd density. We must fix the schedule, not just the staff.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Benjamin, your worry is real. But my contingency pricing shows the ground itself is the hidden delay. Three jobs stopped for weeks on unrecorded voids. We must respect the earth.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, your staffing gap is real. Yet my contract shows lift maintenance has spare capacity. We must choose plans that use existing hands, not demand new ones.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
